## Summary: risk and mitigation
- 30 sequential + 32 CPU-stressed runs (4 parallel workers, 4 busy-loop burners) + 10 randomized orders + per-file/reversed/shared-process/concurrency=4 runs: 0 failures.
- Race tests (TC-08..11, 14) synchronise with createBarrier/deferred (promise gates), not sleeps; no setTimeout, Date.now, Math.random or performance in review tests/helpers.
- Clock injected: createReviewRouter({now}) defaults to new Date() only when not given; helpers pass a fixed FIXED_NOW, so decidedAt is deterministic.
- Residual risk: each test builds its own store + app on port 0 (no shared state, no fixed port). Per-test timeouts (10-20 s) bound hangs; a barrier that never fills would hang to timeout rather than flake. Real loopback HTTP means a pathological OS socket exhaustion could still fail, not observed.
